Package: mica-board-cx3576
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: mica build <mica@example.invalid>
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Depends: mica-system, mica-busybox, kmod, mawk | awk
Provides: mica-board
Conflicts: mica-board
Description: Mica OS hardware and storage policy for CX3576-Z
 FIRMWARE/SYSTEM/DATA storage policy, board hardware initialization,
 radio configuration and status indicators. Kernel, modules, radio firmware
 and boot executables are separate signed components.
 .
 mica-busybox is in Depends for hwinit-mac, which sets the derived Ethernet
 addresses with `busybox ip` inside the udev event: the image carries no
 iproute2. CAN parameters go through systemd-networkd instead.
